+# Grove Swarm Research
+
+This workspace contains project proposals, interactive explanations, research guidance and preserved experimental evidence. **A completed run is not automatically a qualified model experiment or a confirmed scientific result.** The current [principal-investigator review](review-2026-10-04/index.html) distinguishes those states and gives prioritized fixes, a review of all sixteen proposals, and a file-level coverage ledger.
+
+The review covers **1,331 unique project files** across two immutable snapshots: 1,056 files at 2026-10-04 02:30:09 UTC, followed by an addendum of 275 new and 11 updated files at 02:58:11 UTC. Later changes are outside those cutoffs and are listed separately in the review’s drift record. The older [hackathon context](grove-hackathon-context.md) remains a historical planning handoff.
+
+## Start here
+
+- [Experiment-by-experiment PI review](review-2026-10-04/scientific-review.html): all ten named projects, 21 study/version reviews, 110 scenario and condition assessments, eight research areas and all sixteen original proposals. Covers scientific interest, robustness, scenario adequacy, controls, parameters and the next decisive study; includes the latest frozen heterogeneous-swarms revision.
+- [Experimental methodology](agent-experiment-guide/README.md): question, contrast, scoring, uncertainty and evidence preservation.
+- [Agent definition and lifecycle](agent-experiment-guide/AGENT-LIFECYCLE.md): reliable initialization, context assembly, memory, permissions, reset, resume and fork semantics. Recommended contract; production launcher extensions are not yet implemented.
+- [Lifecycle research supplement](agent-experiment-guide/AGENT-LIFECYCLE-RESEARCH.md): 29 annotated papers, engineering articles, essays and social entries, with reading depth and limitations.
+- [Detailed project review](review-2026-10-04/index.html): critical bugs, evidence checks, redesigns, aesthetics and acceptance criteria.
+
+## What each project currently establishes
+
+| Project | Evidence class at review cutoff | Read first |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Collective sensing guide example | Deterministic scripted harness demonstration; 960 saved worlds, not model efficacy evidence | [Protocol](agent-experiment-guide/examples/collective-sensing/PROTOCOL.md), [results](agent-experiment-guide/examples/collective-sensing/RESULTS.md) |
+| Regrowth 200 | Six exploratory completed worlds on one fixed map; shared model policies called through individual controller state; hybrid adds no endpoint gain in this pilot | [Results](regrowth-200/RESULTS.md), [development history](regrowth-200/DEVELOPMENT.md) |
+| Avalon | 45 scripted worlds across three sweeps; real model adapter remains a design | [Results](avalon-swarm/RESULTS.md), [adapter boundary](avalon-swarm/ADAPTER.md) |
+| Swarm of Theseus | Qualified, narrow native-model S1 pilot: 36 condition trajectories in six paired worlds; notes and notes-plus-mentoring reach the task ceiling | [Results](swarm-of-theseus/RESULTS.md), [reviews](swarm-of-theseus/reviews/) |
+| Healing Helping Hands | Pilot01/02 model qualification failures; complete pilot03 export has 72 exact/Jev worlds and 108 Qwen-derived not-run assignments. Jev extraction matches exact; propagation remains programmed | [Evidence directory](healing-helping-hands/results/), [review details](review-2026-10-04/evidence-projects-review.json) |
+| Immune response | Historical instrument: eight native-v2 outcomes with an invalid primary control and 720 scripted-v3 outcomes. New scenarios add 384 unique scripted and 28 native episodes, with poor recovery despite a narrow qualification pass | [Assessment](immune-response-review/REVIEW.md), [agent specification](immune-response-review/AGENT-SPEC.md) |
+
+## Proposals and explanations
+
+[Swarm Ecology Dossier](swarm-ecology-dossier.html) contains sixteen proposals and biological analogies. [Influence guide](swarm-influence-guide.html) is a worked thought experiment with explicitly invented aggregate counts. [SEO poisoning guide](swarm-seo-poisoning-mega-guide.html) contains a numeric surrogate and a proposed model study. These pages are useful explanations; their animations and toy counts are not observed model performance.
+
+## Before a new run
+
+Follow [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md). Write the experimental plan before experimental implementation. Before launch, publish and verify its readable immutable public page; register a condition-specific TLDR covering question, treatment, comparator, metrics and limitations; pass the public-plan preflight. The review identifies bypasses in existing launchers that must be closed before reusing them.
+
+Keep execution status, response-contract validity, scientific qualification, reporting status and process compliance separate. Preserve original outcomes and label later analyses or plans retrospective. Keep credentials entirely outside transcripts and artifacts. Use local secure credential consumption and record only approved names/status.
+
+This review changed conceptual documentation, navigation, one presentation-generation bug and two documented factual corrections. It did not repair all experimental runners, launch model experiments, publish results or modify historical raw outcomes. The HTML review is generated from review JSON by `python3 review-2026-10-04/build_review.py`; rebuilding it performs no experiments.
