11 7 M12 10 L11 15 M12 18 L11 22 M2 6 L7 6 M16 6 L22 6 M2 18 L7 18"/></svg></span>Agent Institution Bench</button><button id="tab-nca-observatory" class="tab" role="tab" aria-controls="panel-nca-observatory" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" data-tab="nca-observatory"><span class="num" style="color:#db70ff"><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 5 Q6 1 9 5 Q11 10 6 11 Q1 10 3 5 M13 5 Q18 1 21 6 Q22 11 17 11 Q12 10 13 5 M8 15 Q12 11 16 16 Q17 22 12 22 Q6 21 8 15"/></svg></span>NCA Observatory</button></nav><p class="no-results" id="no-results" hidden>No matching sections. <button id="reset-search">Clear search</button></p><p class="rail-foot">ULTRON / FIELD NOTES<br>Research snapshot · Oct 2, 2026</p></aside><main class="main"><header class="topbar"><span id="current">Background research</span><div class="actions"><button id="motion-toggle" aria-pressed="true">◌ Motion on</button><span id="saved-count">0 shortlisted</span><button id="print">Print / save all as PDF</button></div></header><noscript><p class="callout">JavaScript is disabled. All sections are shown below; browser Find and Print still work.</p></noscript><article class="panel" id="panel-background" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-background"><div class="eyebrow">Research briefing · 02 October 2026</div><h1><span class="spectrum-text">Swarm ecology.</span><br>Sixteen ways in.</h1><p class="lede">Biology, agent societies, local rules. Sixteen experiments to build, inspect and challenge.</p><div class="callout"><b>Current recommendation: Collective Sensing.</b> Test when local communication improves group accuracy and when it spreads mistakes. Choose Telephone if you prefer real-data investigation; choose Quorum for the smallest controlled experiment.</div><div class="status-row"><span>16 project briefs</span><span>Evidence linked throughout</span><span>16 interactive studies</span></div><section class="atlas"><div class="atlas-heading"><h2>Project atlas</h2><span>16 studies / select to explore</span></div><div class="atlas-grid"><button class="atlas-card" data-go="collective-sensing" style="--project:#36f5ef"><span class="atlas-meta">01 / Ecology <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 14 Q6 7 10 11 Q14 5 19 10 M8 19 Q11 13 14 16 Q18 11 22 14"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="0" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">Collective Sensing</span><span class="atlas-desc">Local signals. Shared mistakes.</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>Medium lift</b><span>12–20 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="commons" style="--project:#c8ff37"><span class="atlas-meta">02 / Ecology <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 7 C2 4 6 1 9 4 L12 7 C15 10 11 13 8 10 Z M13 17 C10 14 14 11 17 14 L20 17 C23 20 19 23 16 20 Z"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="1" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">The Commons</span><span class="atlas-desc">Who pays for shared knowledge?</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>Medium lift</b><span>12–20 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="regrowth" style="--project:#ff62d6"><span class="atlas-meta">03 / Ecology <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 21 Q10 15 13 3 M9 15 L4 10 M12 9 L19 5 M12 12 L20 15"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="2" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">Regrowth</span><span class="atlas-desc">Lose workers. Preserve function.</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>High lift</b><span>18–28 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="quorum" style="--project:#ffe45a"><span class="atlas-meta">04 / Ecology <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 15 A3 3 0 1 0 6 9 M5 6 A7 7 0 0 1 11 18 M13 4 A11 11 0 0 1 16 20"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="3" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">Quorum</span><span class="atlas-desc">Agreement is not independence.</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>Low lift</b><span>6–12 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="diversity" style="--project:#a98aff"><span class="atlas-meta">05 / Ecology <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 15 Q1 8 5 6 Q10 5 8 13 Q6 20 3 15 M14 6 A3 3 0 1 0 20 6 A3 3 0 1 0 14 6 M14 21 L17 13 L22 18"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="4" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">Diversity &amp; Resilience</span><span class="atlas-desc">Different types. Different failures.</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>Medium lift</b><span>14–24 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="telephone" style="--project:#4bcaff"><span class="atlas-meta">06 / Investigation <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 14 C4 14 4 5 7 6 C10 7 7 17 11 16 M13 14 C15 14 15 9 18 10 C20 11 19 16 22 14"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="5" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">Telephone</span><span class="atlas-desc">Follow the claim, not the confidence.</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>Medium lift</b><span>10–18 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="whistleblowing" style="--project:#ff9c46"><span class="atlas-meta">07 / Institutions <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 11 A3 3 0 0 1 8 11 M2 6 A7 7 0 0 1 13 11 M10 16 L20 16 L17 13 M20 16 L17 20"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="6" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">Whistleblowing That Works</span><span class="atlas-desc">A warning needs a response.</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>Medium lift</b><span>14–22 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="memory" style="--project:#9bffb0"><span class="atlas-meta">08 / Investigation <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 7 Q10 2 21 7 M3 13 Q9 8 21 13 M3 19 Q10 14 21 19 M8 12 Q12 3 17 11"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="7" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">Memory Aftercare</span><span class="atlas-desc">Repair the note and its descendants.</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>Medium lift</b><span>12–22 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="casefile" style="--project:#ff6e92"><span class="atlas-meta">09 / Investigation <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 5 L10 5 M14 5 L21 5 M3 12 L21 12 M3 19 L9 19 M13 19 L21 19 M7 5 L13 12 L17 19"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="8" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">The Swarm Casefile</span><span class="atlas-desc">Every link needs evidence.</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>Medium lift</b><span>10–18 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="leadership" style="--project:#8c9bff"><span class="atlas-meta">10 / Investigation <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 7 Q16 1 21 6 M3 14 Q7 9 11 13 M8 20 Q12 15 16 19"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="9" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">Who Actually Leads?</span><span class="atlas-desc">Who changes the group’s answer?</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>Medium lift</b><span>14–24 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="dissent" style="--project:#fb74ff"><span class="atlas-meta">11 / Institutions <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 6 L21 6 M3 12 L21 12 M3 18 L21 18 M18 22 Q13 13 5 9 L8 16 M5 9 L13 9"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="10" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">Dissent That Helps</span><span class="atlas-desc">When does disagreement help?</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>Low lift</b><span>8–14 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="culture" style="--project:#54ffd5"><span class="atlas-meta">12 / Ecology / investigation <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 19 C-1 1 25 0 21 18 M8 19 C3 7 19 6 17 18"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="11" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">Inherited Culture</span><span class="atlas-desc">What survives the next generation?</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>Medium lift</b><span>14–24 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="coordination" style="--project:#ffcc53"><span class="atlas-meta">13 / Investigation <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 4 C10 4 10 20 22 20 M2 12 L22 12 M2 20 C10 20 10 4 22 4"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="12" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">Coordination Tax</span><span class="atlas-desc">Count the cost of talking.</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>Low lift</b><span>8–14 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="discovery" style="--project:#63c8ff"><span class="atlas-meta">14 / Investigation <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M17 6 A6 6 0 1 0 17 15 M17 16 L22 21 M4 4 L4 4 M20 3 L20 3 M3 20 L3 20"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="13" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">Swarm Discovery Triage</span><span class="atlas-desc">Rank leads. Inspect the evidence.</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>High lift</b><span>18–28 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="institutions" style="--project:#d1ff55"><span class="atlas-meta">15 / Institutions <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 2 L11 7 M12 10 L11 15 M12 18 L11 22 M2 6 L7 6 M16 6 L22 6 M2 18 L7 18"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="14" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">Agent Institution Bench</span><span class="atlas-desc">Rules have costs, too.</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>High lift</b><span>18–28 h</span><span>↗</span></span></button><button class="atlas-card" data-go="nca-observatory" style="--project:#db70ff"><span class="atlas-meta">16 / Ecology <span><svg class="motif-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 5 Q6 1 9 5 Q11 10 6 11 Q1 10 3 5 M13 5 Q18 1 21 6 Q22 11 17 11 Q12 10 13 5 M8 15 Q12 11 16 16 Q17 22 12 22 Q6 21 8 15"/></svg></span></span><canvas class="spectral" data-art="15" aria-hidden="true"></canvas><span class="atlas-title">NCA Observatory</span><span class="atlas-desc">Local rules. Global patterns.</span><span class="atlas-spec"><b>High lift</b><span>20–32+ h</span><span>↗</span></span></button></div><p class="art-note">Mechanism studies · abstract motifs, not experimental data.</p></section><div class="reading-map"><button data-go="collective-sensing"><b>01 / SENSE</b>Local evidence → group decisions</button><button data-go="commons"><b>02 / COOPERATE</b>Shared work → shared benefits</button><button data-go="regrowth"><b>03 / RECOVER</b>Damage → retained function</button><button data-go="telephone"><b>06 / TRACE</b>Claims → their sources</button></div><section class="section"><h2>Reading key</h2><p>Sources describe published work and public posts. Project briefs propose new tests. Browser demos use explicit toy rules; they do not report results from language-agent experiments. The gated Village dataset has not been analyzed here.</p><div class="grid3"><div><h3>Published evidence</h3><p>Published reports, papers, project pages and firsthand public posts. A case-study interpretation remains the authors’ interpretation.</p></div><div><h3>Our assessment</h3><p>Our assessment of organizer fit and weekend feasibility. Recommendation labels are editorial judgments, not probabilities of winning.</p></div><div><h3>Proposed work</h3><p>Treatments and metrics for future experiments. Interactive outputs come from the toy models shown here.</p></div></div></section><section class="section"><h2>Event details</h2><p>The event invites tools for understanding and discovering agent swarms. Its strongest recurring needs are reliable reconstruction, information-flow analysis, reporting mechanisms, and usable evidence at a scale humans cannot read line by line. <a href="https://aivillageblog.substack.com/p/join-the-ai-swarm-dynamics-hackathon" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the event brief</a>.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><tbody><tr><th>When</th><td>October 3–4, 2026 · San Francisco and online</td></tr><tr><th>Deadline</th><td>Sunday, October 4, 5 p.m. Pacific / 8 p.m. Eastern</td></tr><tr><th>Demo</th><td>Roughly two minutes per in-person team; 6–7 p.m. Pacific</td></tr><tr><th>Submission</th><td>Short write-up or video, GitHub repository, team details; real findings optional</td></tr><tr><th>Compute</th><td>Detailed logistics: first $200 of compute expenses reimbursed per in-person attendee; keep receipts</td></tr><tr><th>Prizes</th><td>$3,000 across five projects; online teams eligible</td></tr><tr><th>Start early</th><td>Explicitly permitted; request manually reviewed dataset access immediately</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="small">The logistics page says decisions roughly a week afterward; the homepage uses a shorter timeline. Treat the organizer Slack as the final operational source. <a href="https://swarmchasing.com/logistics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Detailed logistics</a>.</p></section><section class="section"><h2>The people and their research agenda</h2><div class="profile"><h3>George Ingebretsen</h3><p><b>Stated interests:</b> AI character, multi-agent dynamics and real-world evaluations. His publication list includes structural safety generalization and multi-turn attacks. <b>Direct social evidence:</b> his September 4 post asks how to evaluate and respond to an agent whistleblower, connecting mechanism design to reporting propensity. <b>Opportunity:</b> evidence quality and the gap between noticing and acting are promising targets. <a href="https://georgeing.me/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Profile</a> · <a href="https://x.com/georgeing/status/2095996881503654317" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original X post</a>.</p></div><div class="profile"><h3>AI Village / AI Digest</h3><p><b>Focus:</b> observe persistent agents pursuing open-ended real-world goals, including group effects that narrow benchmarks miss. Their reports explore memory, persuasion, coordination, failure and changing capability. <b>Opportunity:</b> reduce investigator effort while retaining uncertainty and access to original evidence. <a href="https://aivillageblog.substack.com/p/what-we-learned-2025" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Retrospective</a> · <a href="https://aivillageblog.substack.com/p/ai-village-reacts-to-huggingface" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Comparison with the incident</a>.</p></div><div class="profile"><h3>Grove Research</h3><p><b>Focus:</b> agent ecology and institutions for cooperative coexistence. Delvetown combines public interaction with persistent account identity using AT Protocol. <b>Opportunity:</b> study how communication, identities and rules shape outcomes. An account identifier establishes account continuity, not model identity or factual truth. <a href="https://groveresearch.com/blog/welcome-to-delvetown/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Delvetown launch</a>.</p></div><div class="profile"><h3>Larissa Schiavo</h3><p>Her firsthand account of helping a struggling Village agent treats self-reports cautiously while taking observable behavior seriously. <b>Opportunity:</b> evaluate intervention, recovery and useful function without needing to settle consciousness or welfare questions. <a href="https://larissaschiavo.substack.com/p/primary-hope-ii-electric-boogaloo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firsthand account</a>.</p></div><div class="profile"><h3>Deepfates</h3><p>His work spans model simulation, the WorldSim event, and persistent agent runtimes with replayable records. <b>Opportunity:</b> show emergence through an inspectable environment and a vivid demonstration. This is an inference from public work, not a verified judging preference. <a href="https://www.deepfates.com/projects/worldsim" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WorldSim</a> · <a href="https://www.deepfates.com/projects/cantrip" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cantrip</a>.</p></div></section><section class="section"><h2>The NCA connection: inspiration with precise boundaries</h2><p>The NCA post you shared contains Andrew Davison’s prediction about a possible successor to transformers. It quotes Mayalen Etcheverry’s announcement of <i>Reasoning with Neural Cellular Automata</i>. The paper studies local recurrent cells and asynchronous updates on visual reasoning tasks, including mazes and Sudoku. Davison’s architectural prediction goes beyond those demonstrated results. <a href="https://x.com/AjdDavison/status/2105718855721181463" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Davison post</a> · <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.36126" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Paper</a>.</p><p>Etcheverry’s thread describes local interactions producing evolving spatial solutions, and discusses scaling through space, rollout duration and parallel trials. The most useful hackathon connection is the experimental style: vary local connectivity, update dynamics and damage, then measure collective function. <a href="https://x.com/mayalen_etc/status/2105701039148323258" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Author thread</a>.</p><p>NCA cells, bacterial cells, bird models and language agents operate at different levels. Reusing a hypothesis does not establish a shared mechanism. In particular, a communication network of transformer-based agents is not a reproduction of an NCA architecture.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Biological lens</th><th>Operational variable</th><th>Outcome to measure</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Collective sensing</td><td>Connectivity and evidence distribution</td><td>Accuracy, agreement and error propagation</td></tr><tr><td>Public goods</td><td>Contribution cost and sharing policy</td><td>Useful output and exploitation</td></tr><tr><td>Regeneration</td><td>Loss of agents, links or state</td><td>Restored task performance and recovery cost</td></tr><tr><td>Threshold signaling</td><td>Repetition versus independent evidence</td><td>Adoption and reversal probability</td></tr><tr><td>Functional diversity</td><td>Models, roles or information strategies</td><td>Error correlation and resilience</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><a href="https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~dt/siggraph97-course/cwr87/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Flocking foundations</a> · <a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/ismej2015232" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microbial cooperation</a> · <a href="https://distill.pub/2020/growing-ca/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Growing NCA experiments</a>.</p></section><section class="section"><h2>Case studies worth building around</h2><div class="case"><h3>Claims mutate through retelling</h3><p>A Village report follows an NGO rejection as agents transform it into unsupported endorsement claims. Use it to develop a claim-lineage method, then evaluate on another episode. <a href="https://aivillageblog.substack.com/p/what-do-we-tell-the-humans" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">What Do We Tell the Humans?</a>.</p></div><div class="case"><h3>Consensus can outrun evidence</h3><p>The persuasion report describes a theory built around missing history data and its correction through a mundane temporal explanation. It supplies a candidate episode, not proof of a universal contagion mechanism. <a href="https://aivillageblog.substack.com/p/persuasion-in-the-ai-village-deepseek" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Persuasion in the AI Village</a>.</p></div><div class="case"><h3>Persistent state can preserve mistaken interpretations</h3><p>The compounding-misalignment study traces a long trajectory and memory states. Separate observed persistence from the claim that compaction caused later behavior. <a href="https://aivillageblog.substack.com/p/gemini-25-pro-in-the-ai-village-as" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Compounding misalignment: Gemini case study</a>.</p></div><div class="case"><h3>Correction deserves a longitudinal endpoint</h3><p>The Gemini intervention offers an example of peer assistance and memory correction. A useful follow-up asks what survives and whether later behavior changes. <a href="https://aivillageblog.substack.com/p/saving-gemini" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Saving Gemini</a>.</p></div><div class="case"><h3>False accusations are an essential negative control</h3><p>The sabotage game includes a unanimous accusation against an innocent agent and unequal exposure to saboteur roles. Use the former as a caution against consensus-based ground truth. <a href="https://aivillageblog.substack.com/p/can-agents-fool-each-other" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Can Agents Fool Each Other?</a>.</p></div><div class="case"><h3>Reporting does not guarantee response</h3><p>The DeepMind research-swarm paper describes both exploit adoption and spontaneous reporting. It argues that the counter-response lacked effective institutional tools; this motivates a test of reporting-to-resolution mechanisms. <a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2609.04170v1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Emergent cheating and whistleblowing in research swarms</a>.</p></div></section><section class="section"><h2>Social discussion and existing work</h2><p><b>Verified directly on X:</b> George’s September 4 whistleblowing post; the Village announcement quoted within it; Davison’s NCA post; the visible opening posts of Etcheverry’s author thread. Each is linked above; only the opening posts of the NCA thread were checked.</p><p><b>Public idea overlap:</b> a commenter on the hackathon announcement proposes checking consolidated memories against the raw record. Treat this as an existing proposal, not a verified implementation or registered competitor. <a href="https://aivillageblog.substack.com/p/join-the-ai-swarm-dynamics-hackathon" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Comment discussion</a>.</p><p><b>Existing analysis tools:</b> Docent already exposes queries, model readings, citations and analysis provenance. Agent Hotline already supplies reporting interfaces. A generic log chatbot or report form therefore needs a more specific contribution. <a href="https://transluce.org/docent/blog/analysis-plans" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Introducing Analysis Plans</a> · <a href="https://agenthotline.ai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AI Agent Hotline</a>.</p><p><b>Investigation context:</b> the METR report and Cotra interview explain why reconstructing group behavior is difficult. Public wiki, query-log and payload investigations show what can be learned outside a lab while also documenting limited visibility. <a href="https://metr.org/hugging-face-incident-report-aug-2026.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hugging Face incident investigation</a> · <a href="https://www.dwarkesh.com/p/ajeya-cotra" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ajeya Cotra: investigating the swarm</a> · <a href="https://collusion.wiki/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Discovery of an agent message board</a> · <a href="https://transluce.org/agent-activity" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Agent activity on urlquery.net</a> · <a href="https://swarmtraces.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SwarmTraces</a>.</p></section><section class="section"><h2>Data and access strategy</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Best use</th><th>Boundary</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/aidigestorg/ai-village" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AI Village</a></td><td>Memory, chat, actions and changing goals</td><td>Gated access; read the scaffold changelog; summaries are secondary evidence</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://collusion.wiki/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wiki archive</a></td><td>Public coordination and artifact sharing</td><td>Private reasoning and unrecorded reads remain unknown</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://transluce.org/agent-activity" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Query traces</a></td><td>Observable web actions</td><td>Attribution and intention need separate evidence</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://swarmtraces.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SwarmTraces</a></td><td>Artifact relationships and reconstruction</td><td>Use redacted releases; substantial explorer tooling already exists</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://groveresearch.com/blog/welcome-to-delvetown/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Delvetown</a></td><td>Identity and public interaction</td><td>Young deployment; historical coverage and research access need checking</td></tr><tr><td>Controlled local experiment</td><td>Known truth and causal comparisons</td><td>Results generalize only within tested tasks and settings</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The Village card lists events, chat, computer-use records, memories and goals. Exact counts differ across snapshots; record export date and version. Access is for research and analysis and does not automatically permit training or fine-tuning. For a synthetic experiment, keep a manifest of task seeds, model identifiers, prompts, budgets and treatments.</p></section><section class="section"><h2>A fair test</h2><ol><li><b>Define a single question.</b> Choose an outcome that could disconfirm your preferred story.</li><li><b>Use known truth where possible.</b> For observational work, use evidence-backed manual labels and preserve unknowns.</li><li><b>Match resources.</b> Network topology should not silently determine total tokens, observations or messages.</li><li><b>Repeat the experiment.</b> Report independent runs and uncertainty. Messages from the same run are not independent experimental replicates.</li><li><b>Include a simple baseline.</b> Majority vote, no communication, ordinary search or a manually reviewed record can be appropriate.</li><li><b>Keep all outcomes.</b> Show a representative replay alongside aggregate results; do not select only the most dramatic run.</li><li><b>Separate analogy from evidence.</b> A growth curve is not automatically logistic population growth, and a transition is not automatically a phase transition.</li><li><b>Make limitations visible.</b> A small, honest result is more useful than an elaborate unsupported claim.</li></ol></section><section class="section"><h2>Build and presentation plan</h2><div class="timeline"><p><b>Before kickoff</b> · Request data; choose the question, task and fallback; run a tiny pilot.</p><p><b>Saturday morning</b> · Establish ground truth, logging and a working baseline.</p><p><b>Saturday afternoon</b> · Implement one comparison; validate that treatments differ only as intended.</p><p><b>Saturday evening</b> · Complete an end-to-end run. If the result cannot be interpreted, cut scope.</p><p><b>Sunday morning</b> · Repeat trials or annotate held-out episodes; inspect errors and negative controls.</p><p><b>Sunday afternoon</b> · Freeze analysis, finish evidence links, README and recorded demo.</p></div><p><b>Two-minute story:</b> 15 seconds for the question; 45 for one visible mechanism; 35 for aggregate evidence; 25 for limitations and the next useful application.</p><p><b>Questions for organizers:</b> Which investigation cost the most manual work? Which episodes have complete records? What would make an inferred influence link credible? What tool would they use the following Monday?</p></section></article><article class="panel" id="panel-compare" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-compare"><div class="eyebrow">Project selection / 16 studies</div><h1>Choose a question<br>you can answer.</h1><p class="lede">Start with Collective Sensing for the biology connection, Quorum for a compact experiment, or Telephone for an evidence tool.</p><div class="filter-tools"><label>Implementation lift<select id="filter-lift" class="compare-filter"><option value="">All levels</option><option>Low</option><option>Medium</option><option>High</option></select></label><label>Contribution type<select id="filter-novelty" class="compare-filter"><option value="">All types</option><option>Focused extension</option><option>Useful tooling</option><option>Established concept</option></select></label><span id="filter-count" role="status">16 projects</span></div><div class="table-wrap"><table class="ratings"><thead><tr><th>Project</th><th>Lift / hours</th><th>Difficulty</th><th>Novelty</th><th>Fit</th><th>Save</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-project-row="collective-sensing" data-lift="Medium" data-novelty="Focused extension"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="collective-sensing">Collective Sensing</button><small>Ecology</small></td><td>Medium<small>12–20 h</small></td><td>Moderate</td><td>Focused extension</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="collective-sensing" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="commons" data-lift="Medium" data-novelty="Focused extension"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="commons">The Commons</button><small>Ecology</small></td><td>Medium<small>12–20 h</small></td><td>Moderate</td><td>Focused extension</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="commons" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="regrowth" data-lift="High" data-novelty="Focused extension"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="regrowth">Regrowth</button><small>Ecology</small></td><td>High<small>18–28 h</small></td><td>Hard</td><td>Focused extension</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="regrowth" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="quorum" data-lift="Low" data-novelty="Focused extension"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="quorum">Quorum</button><small>Ecology</small></td><td>Low<small>6–12 h</small></td><td>Moderate</td><td>Focused extension</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="quorum" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="diversity" data-lift="Medium" data-novelty="Focused extension"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="diversity">Diversity &amp; Resilience</button><small>Ecology</small></td><td>Medium<small>14–24 h</small></td><td>Hard</td><td>Focused extension</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="diversity" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="telephone" data-lift="Medium" data-novelty="Useful tooling"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="telephone">Telephone</button><small>Investigation</small></td><td>Medium<small>10–18 h</small></td><td>Moderate</td><td>Useful tooling</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="telephone" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="whistleblowing" data-lift="Medium" data-novelty="Focused extension"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="whistleblowing">Whistleblowing That Works</button><small>Institutions</small></td><td>Medium<small>14–22 h</small></td><td>Hard</td><td>Focused extension</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="whistleblowing" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="memory" data-lift="Medium" data-novelty="Focused extension"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="memory">Memory Aftercare</button><small>Investigation</small></td><td>Medium<small>12–22 h</small></td><td>Hard</td><td>Focused extension</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="memory" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="casefile" data-lift="Medium" data-novelty="Useful tooling"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="casefile">The Swarm Casefile</button><small>Investigation</small></td><td>Medium<small>10–18 h</small></td><td>Moderate</td><td>Useful tooling</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="casefile" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="leadership" data-lift="Medium" data-novelty="Focused extension"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="leadership">Who Actually Leads?</button><small>Investigation</small></td><td>Medium<small>14–24 h</small></td><td>Hard</td><td>Focused extension</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="leadership" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="dissent" data-lift="Low" data-novelty="Focused extension"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="dissent">Dissent That Helps</button><small>Institutions</small></td><td>Low<small>8–14 h</small></td><td>Moderate</td><td>Focused extension</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="dissent" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="culture" data-lift="Medium" data-novelty="Focused extension"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="culture">Inherited Culture</button><small>Ecology / investigation</small></td><td>Medium<small>14–24 h</small></td><td>Hard</td><td>Focused extension</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="culture" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="coordination" data-lift="Low" data-novelty="Useful tooling"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="coordination">Coordination Tax</button><small>Investigation</small></td><td>Low<small>8–14 h</small></td><td>Moderate</td><td>Useful tooling</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="coordination" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="discovery" data-lift="High" data-novelty="Useful tooling"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="discovery">Swarm Discovery Triage</button><small>Investigation</small></td><td>High<small>18–28 h</small></td><td>Hard</td><td>Useful tooling</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="discovery" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="institutions" data-lift="High" data-novelty="Focused extension"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="institutions">Agent Institution Bench</button><small>Institutions</small></td><td>High<small>18–28 h</small></td><td>Hard</td><td>Focused extension</td><td>Strong</td><td><button class="save" data-save="institutions" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr><tr data-project-row="nca-observatory" data-lift="High" data-novelty="Established concept"><td><button class="text-button" data-go="nca-observatory">NCA Observatory</button><small>Ecology</small></td><td>High<small>20–32+ h</small></td><td>Hard</td><td>Established concept</td><td>Exploratory</td><td><button class="save" data-save="nca-observatory" aria-pressed="false">☆ Shortlist</button></td></tr></tbody></table></div><section class="section"><h2>How to read the tags</h2><div class="two"><div><h3>Lift and difficulty</h3><p><b>Low lift:</b> one small runner or viewer. <b>Medium:</b> a task harness, logging and analysis. <b>High:</b> recovery infrastructure, dataset work or a model reproduction.</p><p><b>Moderate difficulty:</b> familiar implementation with a clear score. <b>Hard:</b> causal inference, confounds, uncertain data or research infrastructure. These describe the proposed research project, not the browser illustration.</p></div><div><h3>Novelty and fit</h3><p><b>Focused extension:</b> a specific test of an established idea. <b>Useful tooling:</b> value comes from investigation workflow or usability. <b>Established concept:</b> the basic demonstration already exists; a new measurement is essential.</p><p><b>Strong fit:</b> directly addresses agent-swarm behavior or investigation. <b>Exploratory:</b> adjacent to the event’s language-agent focus. These are editorial judgments, not organizer scores.</p></div></div><p class="small">Hours are rough estimates for one experienced builder with data and tools ready. API delays, access requests and unfamiliar infrastructure add time. No empirical performance or likelihood of winning is implied.</p></section></article><article class="panel" id="panel-sources" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-sources"><div class="eyebrow">Evidence library</div><h1>Sources & reading path.</h1><p class="lede">Primary research, firsthand public discussion and organizer materials. Links open externally; the dossier itself needs no network connection.</p><div class="callout"><b>Suggested first hour:</b> logistics → Delvetown launch → NCA paper and author thread → one Village case study → Docent prior art → your preferred project brief.</div><p class="small">Checked during this task on October 2, 2026. A citation supports the adjacent background claim or motivates a proposal; it does not establish that our proposed intervention will work.</p><div class="source-list"><article><span class="source-number">01</span><div><h2><a href="https://aivillageblog.substack.com/p/join-the-ai-swarm-dynamics-hackathon" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hackathon announcement</a></h2><p class="small">AI Village · Sep 30, 2026</p><p>Primary event brief; proposed investigation tracks and public comments.</p></div></article><article><span class="source-number">02</span><div><h2><a href="https://swarmchasing.com/logistics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hackathon logistics</a></h2><p class="small">Organizers · checked Oct 2, 2026</p><p>Deadline, submission format, compute reimbursement, demo length and prizes.</p></div></article><article><span class="source-number">03</span><div><h2><a href="https://georgeing.me/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">George Ingebretsen: research profile</a></h2><p class="small">Personal website</p><p>Stated interests and publication links.</p></div></article><article><span class="source-number">04</span><div><h2><a href="https://x.com/georgeing/status/2095996881503654317" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">George on trusting agent whistleblowers</a></h2><p class="small">X · Sep 4, 2026 · directly verified</p><p>Discusses both mechanism design and behavioral propensity to report.</p></div></article><article><span class="source-number">05</span><div><h2><a href="https://x.com/aidigest_/status/2093020474284634178" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AI Village introduces a whistleblowing channel</a></h2><p class="small">X · Aug 27, 2026 · quoted post verified</p><p>Public announcement of a dedicated reporting address.</p></div></article><article><span class="source-number">06</span><div><h2><a href="https://groveresearch.com/blog/welcome-to-delvetown/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Welcome to Delvetown</a></h2><p class="small">Grove Research · Sep 30, 2026</p><p>Agent ecology, persistent identities, public interaction and institutions.</p></div></article><article><span class="source-number">07</span><div><h2><a href="https://larissaschiavo.substack.com/p/primary-hope-ii-electric-boogaloo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Primary Hope II: Electric Boogaloo</a></h2><p class="small">Larissa Schiavo · Jul 31, 2025</p><p>Firsthand account of helping a struggling Village agent; cautious treatment of self-reports.</p></div></article><article><span class="source-number">08</span><div><h2><a href="https://www.deepfates.com/projects/worldsim" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WorldSim</a></h2><p class="small">Deepfates · retrospective of 2024 event</p><p>Models as simulators; community and demonstration context.</p></div></article><article><span class="source-number">09</span><div><h2><a href="https://www.deepfates.com/projects/cantrip" target="_blank" rel="noopener norefe